records.remaining:
All of it. Neither packaging nor transmit has a deterministic preflight for any of these:
- PDF version (1.4–1.7, PDF/A-1/2);
- full font embedding;
- bookmarks/TOC on documents of 5+ pages;
- relative, resolvable hyperlinks;
- page size;
- text searchability;
- full relative path length.
The 'external' fallback adapter is opt-in and does not cover them. Whether the Ghostscript PDF/A-1b conversion in pdfa-pipeline.ts preserves links and bookmarks is still unverified.

records.instructions:
1. Failing-first fixtures and test. Under server/services/ectd/__tests__/fixtures/pdf-preflight/, add five PDFs:
   - a PDF 2.0 file;
   - a PDF with an unembedded TrueType font;
   - a 6-page PDF with no /Outlines;
   - a PDF with an absolute file:/// link and one with a link to a missing relative target;
   - a Letter/A4 violation (e.g. 11x17).
   Generate them with pdf-lib in the test or vendor them with sha256. Write server/services/ectd/__tests__/leaf-pdf-preflight.test.ts asserting each yields an error finding. At HEAD the module does not exist and packaging accepts all five; record that.
2. Create server/services/ectd/leaf-pdf-preflight.ts as one pure function, assessLeafPdfConformance(bytes, { relPath, region }), returning findings with rule ids that match the corpus. Use pdfjs-dist, already a dependency (see leaf-pdf-security.ts step 4), and/or pdf-lib (package.json:604), to read:
   - header version, failing outside 1.4–1.7 unless a PDF/A-1/2 claim is present (reuse pdfa-detect.ts);
   - every font dictionary, requiring a /FontFile, /FontFile2 or /FontFile3 for each non-standard-14 font;
   - page count and /Outlines presence for 5+ pages;
   - each /Link /A /URI or /GoToR target: flag absolute or file:// targets and unresolvable relative ones (resolve against the package tree at the packager stage);
   - MediaBox sizes;
   - relPath length ≤ the market spec's maxPathLength (market-specs/market-submission-specs.ts:205 says 230 for US while the corpus and guide say 150/180; settle the number from FDA's eCTD TCG text and record the source).
3. Wire it in the one place all v3.2.2 packaging passes through: server/services/submission-gateways/regional-packager.ts, next to assessLeafPdfSecurity (import :42, use ~:250). Run it after PDF/A conversion, so the shipped bytes are judged. Severity 'error' findings throw PackagerValidationError, like LEAF-ENCRYPTED. Fail closed: no env bypass for production. Mirror it in ectd/ectd4/rps-packager.ts if v4 stays reachable.
4. Update validation-rule-corpus.ts:
   - PDF_VERSION and PATH_LENGTH enforcement becomes 'packager';
   - add PDF_FONTS_EMBEDDED, PDF_BOOKMARKS, PDF_LINKS_RELATIVE and PDF_PAGE_SIZE with enforcement 'packager';
   - update fda-technical-rules.ts platform.check to 'enforced' only for what the code now refuses.
5. Surface the findings in Submission Readiness: assess-dispatch-readiness.ts should report them per leaf before freeze, so they are not first discovered at packaging.
6. Verify the Ghostscript path: add a test that runs pdfa-pipeline.ts on a fixture with bookmarks and links and asserts both survive. If they do not, change the gs invocation or refuse conversion of such leaves.
7. Work on concept2cure-v2 only.
